+- DECISION (part 2): kept and documented, not deleted. The subsumption is real — `decodeStrict` refuses non-UTF-8 input before any value exists — but it is a package-internal invariant, not a property of the eight validators. `CanonicalByteLength(value any)` already shows this package can export a non-`[]byte` entry point, so a future map-taking entry would silently make all eight comments false. Deleting would also rewrite refusal statements pinned in `refusal_guards_test.go`.
